WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.790
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic, CECS Department, Cal State Long Beach. Today we are going to

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:11.510
talk about addition and subtraction. So to start with, we are going to do a little bit

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:23.270
of recap as we briefly introduced this topic. And we are going to do, I'm sorry, arithmetic

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:35.310
addition. Addition is one of arithmetic operations. And think about that when we start talking

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:46.230
about arithmetic operators in Verilog in the lab. So rules, as we said previously, if this

00:00:46.230 --> 00:01:00.950
is a and this is b and a plus b, we are going to put sum here and carry over here. If a and

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:15.240
b are both zero, sum is zero, carry is zero. If a or b, only one of them is one, sum is

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:26.360
one, carry is zero. Most interesting case is where both of them are one. Then sum is

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:35.400
zero and carry is one. This is very very similar to regular decimal addition so

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.960
remember this is we are talking about addition in number two I mean base two

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:56.120
systems. Let's do another recap of example so let's work on zero zero one

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:10.920
0 and 0, 0, 1, 0. 0 and 0 is 0, carry is 0. 0 and 1 and 1 is result 0, carry 1. 1 and

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:22.440
2 zeros is 1, carry 0, 3 zeros, sorry, I forgot. 3 zeros are 0 and this is the result. Example

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:42.580
number 2 would be, let's look at these numbers, 0, 1, 1, 1 and 0, 1, 0, 0 from right to left.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:03:06.370
1 and 0 is 1. Carry 0. 0 and 1 and 1 is 0. Carry 1. Two 1's is 0. Carry 1. And then 1, 1 and two 0's is 1. This is the result.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:12.370
However, we have also some interesting things over here.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:20.480
and the interesting thing is called overflow.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.900
Something cannot fit that what overflow is.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.500
Let us think about bits in hardware.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:35.320
So if we have four bit number,

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:39.660
that means that we have four little locations in memory,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.840
each a bit wide, that we are storing the number.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.520
Okay, so we will give an example

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.920
of adding two four bit numbers.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.120
and the example is

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.000
one zero zero zero

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:57.660
and one zero zero zero

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:02.220
so I'm expecting one two three four bits of my result

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.940
zero and zero is zero carry zero

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.760
zero and zero is zero

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.260
carry another zero

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.060
three zeros is zero

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.160
carry zero

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:18.220
one and one is zero

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.880
carry one

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.880
uh oh

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.320
now we have

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.600
a problem

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.720
because we have physical location for four bits

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.440
and suddenly our result actually is five bits.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.320
So these four bits are going to be stored as a result.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:54.980
But this one bit here, that one is going to indicate

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:04.410
that there is an overflow.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.350
So basically the result that we have stored

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.660
is not a correct result.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.240
Important thing to notice,

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.880
because we will be talking about

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.760
all sorts of kinds of overflows is,

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:29.230
right now, this seems unsigned addition,

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:35.220
and for unsigned addition,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:39.980
overflow is also carry from the most significant bit.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:49.080
There is an overflow,

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.240
if carry out from most significant bit,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:06:05.240
that that one here is equal to 1 and a no overflow if that carry is equal to 0.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.240
Hope this was helpful.

